cbfstool (MrChromebox util build, 2021-09-21)

The cbfstool binary MrChromebox publishes for firmware-util.sh, not a Fedora
package (Fedora ships no cbfstool/coreboot RPM). Upstream downloads the same
tarball at run time in functions.sh:get_cbfstool(); the image vendors it so the
persist stage never fetches an executable at run time. Taken verbatim from
https://www.mrchromebox.tech/files/util/cbfstool.tar.gz (the tarball holds a
single `cbfstool` binary; SHA256 records its checksum).

The image extracts it to /usr/lib/pixel-blue/mrchromebox/cbfstool. It is a
dynamically linked glibc build whose only shared-library dependency is libc, so
it runs unmodified on the Fedora image; build_files/modules/42-firmware.sh runs
it after extraction and fails the build if it cannot start.

Refresh by downloading a new tarball from the same directory, replacing
cbfstool.tar.gz, regenerating SHA256 and updating this file; then verify that
42-firmware.sh's smoke test still passes and that the flags the persist stage
uses (`add`, `extract`, `read -r`, `write -r`, `-t raw`) are unchanged.
